  "description": "Temporary display of 2 x externally illuminated shroud advertisements (20m wide x 13.6m high and 10m wide x 13.6m high respectively)&nbsp;inset within a printed decorative mural depicting a green wall",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Hoxton East and Shoreditch Ward",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-18T11:16:31.461Z",
  "street_name": "GREAT EASTERN STREET",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed advertisements, by virtue of their scale, design and positioning, are considered to be harmful to visual amenity insofar as they would be harmful to the character and appearance of the wider streetscene and the South Shoreditch Conservation Area. As such the proposal is contrary to policies D1 (London’s form, character and capacity for growth), D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), (D8 Public Realm) and HC1 (Heritage Conservation and Growth) of the London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character), LP3 (Designated Heritage Assets) and LP7 (Advertisements) of the Hackney Local Plan (2020)."
